t(28, 60, """and his delusion that he is in the right, although he was debated at length and a great deal of time was spent on him at the expense of self and personal life, yet he is a sinful aggressor, I say, counting all the harm that comes to us as reward with our Avenging Lord: the Prophet ﷺ has vouched for this servant in need of Allah the Exalted in true visions, part of which has occurred and come true while part remains, so it was established that they were visions from Allah the Exalted. Above that there were visions with Allah the Almighty our Lord about a state and standing of mine as a servant with Allah the Almighty our Lord; those who heard them from me know them, and I will not repeat them after today. And beneath all this in the worth and rank of visions — after what occurred of a state with Allah the Exalted, which are the visions of highest value, and after the praise, commendation and great love that came in my visions of the Prophet ﷺ, which are the visions ranked second after the visions of the state with Allah the Exalted — there came to me, in the third degree of visions, more than one Muslim man and woman, over periods lasting years from 2011 until 2026, with visions they had seen. To one of them came the martyr who died upon monotheism, saying to him: the owner of this channel is upon the truth; one saw a vision containing a direct command to hold fast to this ship; one saw a vision containing commendation of the assembly; and one saw a vision containing commendation of the one whom Allah enabled to establish this assembly. Over long years of people's correspondence, since the days of the forums in 2011 (so the matter is not new at all), visions have reached me containing commendation of this servant in need of Allah the Exalted, of his method and his way, since that distant time. But I broadcast none of them, neither today nor tomorrow, because what matters is not the servant in need of Allah the Exalted. What matters is that we reach what our Almighty Lord wants from all of us.
And what matters is that we please Allah the Almighty our Lord with us, for the abode of this world holds no recompense for deeds and no reward; the reward is only in the Hereafter. So whoever finds in this assembly an evil ((for which there is clear proof)), let him not fear, for Allah's sake, the blame of any blamer, and let him cast the founder of this assembly aside. And whoever comes without proof or ((imagines a proof)) has transgressed, and whoever transgresses has no place among us on the deck of this ship ever, because no unjust man or unjust woman should ever board it.""")

