t(33, 250, """Every feeling of the heart on which the denial of an established right of people is built is a transgression .. and every feeling of the heart that does not conflict with denying an established right among people's rights holds no transgression. If your heart feels something that does not result in denying an established right of a person, then feel as you wish and at every time! Feel by day and by night, morning and evening, on feast days, on occasions and at other times! But if your heart feels what it feels and that results in injustice or the denial of an established right of people, then you are afflicted with all ten, five on the right and five on the left!""")

t(33, 795, """Do not say: my heart's feeling told me this is right and that is wrong, until you submit your heart's feeling to reason. If reason agrees with a legal text in the Book and the Sunnah, then reason is right and the heart's feeling is right; both are right together! If you submit your heart's feeling to reason and it rejects it, and your reason's rejection matches a legal text that sides with your reason against your heart's feeling, then your reason is right and your feeling is wrong! And if you submit your heart's feeling to reason and it accepts it, and that conflicts with a legal text, then your feeling is wrong and your reason is wrong! Both are wrong together!""")

