t(38, 1510, """The Chinese war doctrine .. Has China expanded before and gone out of Asia? The answer is no

The Mongols were not Chinese and are not the Chinese of today, even though they intermarried after invading and seizing China. China, unlike other nations, has never before gone out to conquer the lands of the world as the Mongols, the Europeans, the Arabs and then the Turks and the Russians did.

The current Chinese doctrine is still as it is. The Chinese are in China. As for the Chinese doctrine after the Third World War, my reading is that it will change. It seems, and Allah knows best, that a movement in Chinese political culture after the Third World War will give rise to a revolution in Chinese political thought that will make the Chinese, for the first time, think of invading outside their lands!

From here, and Allah knows best, begins the idea of the enemy who is behind you! The re-production of Chinese political thought in a state of demolition and rebuilding, due to a deep, terrifying and major civilizational shock, is very possible if present-day China is exposed in the Third World War to a shock on the scale of the shocks that change a person's concept of all of life .. And when a person's concept of all of life changes, he becomes either one of the greatest reformers of the Earth or one of the worst corrupters in it!""")

t(39, 80, """O Muslims: do not buy zero fat - fat-free products, for they are extremely dangerous to the body's health

To make up for the lack of taste and texture after removing the fat from milk or its derivatives, some companies add larger amounts of added sugar or artificial sweeteners and preservatives, and this may lead to:
- A sudden rise in blood sugar.
- A slowing of the metabolic rate, which may cause fat to accumulate in other places in the body.

Dairy naturally contains fat-soluble vitamins such as (A, D, E, K). In the absence of fat when you buy zero fat, the body finds great difficulty in absorbing these vitamins, even if the products are artificially fortified with them.

The natural fats in milk and yogurt help release the satiety hormones. When consuming "zero fat" products, you may feel hungry faster, which pushes you to eat larger amounts of food or sweets later.

Research published in 2025 showed that consuming full-fat dairy (such as cheese and yogurt) may be linked to a lower risk of heart disease and type 2 diabetes compared with the fat-free versions.""")

t(39, 1310, """In brief .. A brother is angry because he does not accept my criticism of the Islamic groups whose thought he embraces .. I was asleep and woke up to his accusation that I had offended the Prophet ﷺ in the post on political speeches, when I said calm political speeches are proof of the ruler's strength. He said: "You offend the Prophet, because his anger used to grow intense on the pulpit, and you are thus telling people the Prophet was not strong." The matter is at root an accusation due to a personal quarrel from a person who has a personal enmity toward me.

The post on calm political speeches, which I published about 23 hours ago, is a post that has not been edited since it was published, and that is a wonder, because 99.9% of my posts I am forced to edit for a spelling mistake that occurs here or there while I write, yet this very post through which you tried to accuse me has had no edit! Does that not stir in you any sign of wonder? This is so that you know you are mistaken and a slanderer, and this is what our Almighty Lord does when He wills to plot against a person who does not fear Allah regarding himself .. And the quarrelsome, disputing brother seems unable to read well what his eyes see, for in the post, whose content has undergone no edit, it is written clearly that from my opinion on the calm political speech which I see as correct (the Friday sermon) is excepted!! But his eyes did not see this sentence!!

So his rashness landed him in a predicament .. I excepted the Friday sermon in the post because it has a context different from political speeches directed at the outside world, and because the Friday sermon is directed inward, for it is admonition and guidance for the Muslim society, not for the global society ... and addressing the inside differs from addressing the outside in calm political speeches .. But Allah the Exalted put this disputant, who disobeys his Prophet ﷺ, in a tight spot by making the post, contrary to habit, unedited, so that the presence of the exception in my words would be proof against you and the proof of accusing without right would be established against you! How did your eyes not see the exception I made for (the Friday sermon)? I know, by the grace of Allah the Exalted, that the Prophet ﷺ, when he spoke in the Friday sermon and treated an error in the Muslim society, would become angry; to Allah belong the praise and the grace, I know that. But because of your personal quarrel Allah blinded you so that you would not see the sentence that leaves my words without the gap you thought, so you said: show me how you will get yourself out of this tight spot? What tight spot, you poor man, when the post is clear in excepting (the Friday sermon)?!

The brother is angry because he came days ago and argued about the thought of the Islamic groups, to one of which he belongs. He was answered in a single reply from me, did not like my reply and responded with a lengthy reply. This is a method I know; it is the method of those who have nothing in""")

t(40, 60, """their lives to do, and whose life, masha'Allah, has 500 hours in the day. My day has only 24 hours. I am not like you. So when he was blocked to prevent the argument, he got angry, entered with another account and said to me: you are bankrupt. I am used to turning away from the ignorant rather than returning the insult or explaining their error, so I blocked him without a reply and said: carry it with you in your record. Then today he returned with a new account, imagining that I had made a grave mistake in the political speech post 22 hours ago and had offended the Prophet ﷺ, because he simply read the post in haste and Allah landed him in the embarrassment of not having read the phrase (except on Friday). So he came imagining he had caught me in a mistake and embarrassed himself.

As for why I blocked you, the answer is:
1- Because the argument you tried to drag me into is in plain violation of the Prophet's ﷺ command to abandon argument. So how do you speak about the religion and disobey your Prophet?
2- My applying the block is not an insult to you but an application of the Prophet's ﷺ command to abandon argument. If I do not apply the Prophet's ﷺ command to you, do I not have the right to apply it to myself and block you so that I am not dragged into argument? If you do not care to listen to your Prophet's words and obey him, you have no right to impose on me that I not obey my Prophet ﷺ, for you do not control me or what I want.
3- The brother considered his being blocked an injustice to him, so he wrote and said that he is my adversary on the Day of Resurrection because I blocked him! No .. You are deluded .. I am not your adversary nor anything, Allah the Exalted willing, because you did not inherit this assembly! This assembly is not an open market that you enter and do in it what you wish! Your right to be in it whatever you do, without being held to account when you err, is a delusion you have deluded yourself with and is not a right at all! And I am not responsible for a person who fabricates delusions about something.

After I blocked you the first time, I became an enemy to you. I do not care about love or hatred!

This is a reply to you and not to the channel's followers""")

